# A linked WhatsApp session is a LIVE CREDENTIAL — anyone who copies it
# controls the account until the device is unlinked. It appears next to the
# server as soon as anyone links. Never commit it.
server/.wwebjs_auth/
server/.wwebjs_cache/
.wwebjs_auth/
.wwebjs_cache/
.env

# The leading slash is load-bearing: it ignores ONLY a root-level node_modules,
# never server/node_modules/. puppeteer cannot be bundled and whatsapp-web.js
# requires it eagerly at load, so a clone WITHOUT server/node_modules crashes on
# startup with "Cannot find module 'puppeteer'". The Claude Code plugin route
# (/plugin install) installs by CLONING this repo, so server/node_modules/ MUST
# be committed and runnable — a bare `node_modules/` here silently breaks that
# entire install path while the .mcpb download keeps working.
/node_modules/
